{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use small deterministic specifications to bind sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe exploratory or recovery action. Clear/search behavior defaults to random_walk, obstacle states force one-shot directed turns, and path_clear returns quickly to exploration while action states self-loop on non-critical path_clear to respect open-loop pulse execution.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in plant automata",
    "Use one policy specification with clear, left-obstacle, right-obstacle, and front-obstacle recovery states plus one-shot action commit states",
    "Bias toward coverage by using random_walk in clear exploration and a short move_forward only after a successful turn recovery",
    "Keep obstacle recovery conservative: no move_forward or random_walk in any obstacle-reached state, and use full_rotate only as a last-resort blocked-front recovery"
  ],
